  "original_description": "Drive a running Claude Code (CC) terminal session as a manager from Cowork \u2014 write directives, trigger phases, approve permission prompts, monitor progress, recover from hangs, and maintain full understanding of the codebase being built. Use this skill any time the user asks Cowork to \"drive Claude Code\", \"manage a development run\", \"automate Claude Code\", \"build a project end-to-end via Claude Code\", \"control my CC session\", or hands you a long-running multi-phase implementation that another agent should execute. Use it even if the user only mentions \"talking to Claude Code from here\" or \"use Claude Code to build it\" \u2014 this skill turns those casual asks into a controlled, observable, recoverable engineering process. The skill bundles macOS AppleScript bridge scripts (paste-with-verify, terminal-buffer reader, single-key sender, permission-prompt watchdog, hang-nudger), file-based directive patterns that bypass paste-truncation issues, hang/recovery procedures, and a checklist for keeping Cowork's own understanding of the project in lockstep with what CC actually built (git log, file diffs, test counts, deferred items).",
